ors alerted the court to the  issue wednesday and requested a hearing  but maxwell's attorney said in a letter  that a hearing wasn't necessary because  a new trial was warranted based on the  juror's statements alone maxwell was  convicted on five of six counts last  month relating to sex trafficking young  girls she is a former girlfriend of  convicted sex offender jeffrey epstein  juror 50's lawyer has not responded to  law and crime's request for comment  here to explain the possible appeal  issues in the maxwell case is criminal  defense attorney nemo romani and co-host  terry austin terry what are the  arguments you suspect maxwell's team  will raise and are they strong ones  i think they're fairly strong brian the  defense is trying to vacate these guilty  verdicts they're claiming during  misconduct and actually they have a very  good case  two jurors have now said they may have  been victims of sexual abuse and they  did not mention that during their  questionnaire and they discussed these  experience during the deliberations and  in fact one juror was trying to convince  the rest of the jury about his  experiences saying that he believed the  witnesses even though the witnesses  might not have remembered everything and  frankly they're not supposed to serve as  experts there's a good chance that this  really could be vacated now nima can we  actually see a new trial or could this  be a strong negotiation tool for maxwell  to seek a better deal  i think we will see a new trial and this  is why the department of justice you  cannot give elaine maxwell the break  especially after what happened when alex  acosta was u.s attorney and he gave jeff  epstein that sweetheart deal where he  barely served any local time he  obviously died never received the  criminal justice that he deserved so you  want to do right by these victims even  if you have to retry the case if you're  the u.s attorney's office that's what  you do to finally bring some closure for  this really heinous sexual abuse ring  that took place over decades  all right we may be seeing then a gi  lane maxilla charge uh coming up and  maybe a trial part two will of course  give you updates as this argument for a  new trial continues when we come back  one year since the january 6 attacks an  investigation is still ongoing the  latest from the january 6 committee and  president joe biden's comments on the  one-year anniversary  welcome back to log in crime daily  thursday marks the one year anniversary  of the january 6 2021 insurrection in  washington d.c where a mob swarmed the  u.s capitol in an effort to overthrow  the results of the 2020 presidential  election  one year later the so-called january 6  committee is still investigating the  attacks most recently contacting fox  news host sean hannity about the  incident as long crime daily has  reported messages between hannity and  several other fox news hosts were sent  to former president trump and then chief  of staff mark meadows condemning the  attack the committee has also been in  contact with former vice president mike  pence who certified the 2020  presidential election results they say  he is cooperating with the investigation  on thursday president joe biden  addressed the attacks saying it was a  threat on the foundation of america's  rule of law  the will of the people was under assault  the constitution our constitution  faced  the gravest of threats  outnumbered in the face of the brutal  attack  the capitol police  the d.c metropolitan police department  the national guard  another brave law enforcement officials  saved the rule of law  our democracy held  we the people endured  we the people prevailed  for the first time in our history  a president  had not just lost an election  he tried to prevent the peaceful  transfer of power  as a violent mob breached the capital  but they failed  they failed  on this day of remembrance we must make  sure that such attack never never  happens again  what do you make of the investigation  into the insurrection now that a year  has passed and what grade would you give  it  brian i would give the department of  justice a solid b and this is why  they've done a good job identifying  almost all the people that unlawfully  enter the capitol building using social  media some of them were stupid enough to  stream it while they were breaking the  law and snitches and also they've gotten  to the next level folks that weren't  there but that were leading the  insurrection the proud boys the three  percenters the oath keepers the reason i  don't give them an a is just the slow  pace of the us attorney's office now  obviously federal prosecutors they're  not used to handling this volume of  cases but i would have expected at least  one or more of the cases to have gone to  trial  after a year  anniversary of the capital rights right  i think some of the trials are coming up  i think maybe in a few weeks so let's  see if they can get an a in your books  terry your reaction to president biden's  remarks did he hit the right point in  the proper tone for the seriousness of  this anniversary  brian he absolutely hit the right point  and the proper tone his remarks today  were the strongest to date on the  subject while he didn't mention trump by  name he definitely referred to the  former president multiple times and one  of the things i think he was trying to  do is to basically set the stage for the  next presidential election he's trying  to say that he is the right person for  this country and trump is not trump  cannot put himself above the law which  is one of the things biden was saying  that trump was trying to do here and  basically he cannot keep attacking  democracy we all have to make sure that  we protect what our country is standing  for which obviously is for democracy and  we cannot allow this to happen again so  one of the lines that he said that i  thought was really good is that you  can't put yourself above the 